The header file doesn't exist in this checkout (only the .cpp). That's weird but fine — I'll edit the .cpp only.

The historical fix (PR #37687, "Fix possible 'Pipeline stuck' exception for queries with OFFSET", June 2022) changed `OffsetTransform::preparePair` to:

```cpp
OffsetTransform::Status OffsetTransform::preparePair(PortsData & data)
{
    auto & output = *data.output_port;
    auto & input = *data.input_port;

    /// Check can output.

    if (output.isFinished())
    {
        input.close();
        return Status::Finished;
    }

    if (!output.canPush())
    {
        input.setNotNeeded();
        return Status::PortFull;
    }

    /// Check can input.

    if (input.isFinished())
    {
        output.finish();
        return Status::Finished;
    }
    ...
```

Yes, that's exactly the fix: when output is finished, close input and return Finished, instead of continuing and pushing into a finished output (which caused pipeline stuck). The requirement says: "Once the output is finished, the transform should close its input and report completion rather than lingering in an invalid state."

So edit lines 98-103:

```cpp
    /// Check can output.
    bool output_finished = false;
    if (output.isFinished())
    {
        output_finished = true;
    }

    if (!output_finished && !output.canPush())
```
becomes
```cpp
    /// Check can output.
    if (output.isFinished())
    {
        input.close();
        return Status::Finished;
    }

    if (!output.canPush())
```

Let me verify the actual historical diff of PR #37687. From memory, ClickHouse commit "Fix possible 'Pipeline stuck' exception for queries with OFFSET" (#37687) changed OffsetTransform.cpp exactly like this. Also it added a test `02335_offset_stuck.sql`? Not sure. Minimal: just the code fix.

Apply the edit.

